From: mscharged-port
Subject: Convert native time-up checks the way MWCC does
Upstream-base: 9046e67aa2077a7eb4ed6e28c9df3c1d3b368f84
Classification: native compiler/ABI compatibility

Game, StatsTracker and Presentation detect the end of regulation time with
(unsigned int)(10.0f * (duration - gameTime)) == 0. The game clock keeps
running past the duration (its end time is 999999), so in sudden death and
while a shot holds the whistle the remainder is negative. MWCC's
__cvt_fp2unsigned turns any negative value into 0, so retail keeps treating
that time as up; on x86-64 the conversion is undefined and yields a large
nonzero word. Natively a sudden death goal then played the ordinary goal
celebration, skipped StatsTracker::TrackWinner (final score and series wins
stayed 0-0, and the Striker Times paired the away captain with itself), and
the time-up test only held within a tenth of a second of the whistle, so a
shot still active then let the match run on.

Natively the five checks use VariantFloatToWiiWord, the existing replica of
__cvt_fp2unsigned.

